Here's what I found for 6 Larch Grove:

**Constraints:** The property is not in a conservation area, is not a listed building, and has no tree preservation order. That means the usual restrictions that tighten the rules don't apply.

**Council guidance on outbuildings:** Garden rooms and sheds generally do not need a planning application if they meet all of these conditions:
- No more than 2.5 metres high
- Located behind the front wall of the house
- Covering less than half the garden area

**What this means for you:** If your garden room meets all three conditions, it probably doesn't need an application. If it's taller than 2.5 metres, sits forward of the front wall, or would cover half or more of the garden, you would likely need one.

I can't give a formal planning opinion, so please confirm the details with the council before you build. If you can tell me the proposed height, its position relative to the house, and roughly how much of the garden it would cover, I can help you check it against those conditions. If you're unsure, the council can give you a definitive answer, and I can also look up any existing applications for the address if you have a reference.
